What does System.out print, apart from the separately configured logger output?

Environment: JShell or a Java class. The logger also emits a configured log record; its timestamp, format, and destination depend on the runtime logging configuration.

```java
// A local observability exercise using a JDK logger.
var logger = System.getLogger("expenses");
String requestId = "req-42";
logger.log(System.Logger.Level.INFO, "request_id={0} operation={1}", requestId, "expense_created");
System.out.println("request tracked: " + requestId);
```
